{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"850779383656218636","content":"so warlock vs cleric, vs paladin is a really nuanced and weird thing..... but basically one way or another you are granted access to raw power, and you shape it.\n\nAn eldritch blast can manifest as eye lasers, or finger guns, or spectral arrows fired from a ghostly bow, etc..... its how you shape the power with your will into effect.  Basically all warlock spells would be similar\n\ncleric, a diety is granting you access to divine power, so all the magic should be shaped/flavored based on the god at hand (so for instance if your god is Zeus, then lots of lightning and thunder flavor would be approprate, whereas hephestus, might manifest with the sound of a hammer on anvil or some such.  Clerics devoted to a domain without god, would likely still be flavored on what the core of that domain is)\n\nPaladins are no longer really holy.... instead they are devoted so hard to their oaths, various gods are likely to justgrant them power.  As such the oath would likely flavor the magic (so a summoned steed for oath of vengance might look more like a nightmare, whereas order of nature might be an elk)","created_at":"2021-08-03T13:06:30.084000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"872103134191824956","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
